      "body": "Assisted-by: OpenAI Codex\n\n\n\n## Overview\n\nDo not send a normal completion request after streaming-input processing fails.\nUnder asynchronous scheduling, it can race with the failed session's abort under the same request ID.\n\nThis is distinct from [#49722](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/49722), which handles a valid terminal request, and [#51900](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51900), which caps cumulative session length. No duplicate open PR was found on 2026-10-21.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Input errors still reach the caller, but no final request is submitted after failure.\n- Normal completion and cancellation remain unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nOn main `64c5f14` with this change:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/v1/streaming_input/test_async_llm_streaming.py -q  # 8 passed\n.venv/bin/pre-commit run --files vllm/v1/engine/async_llm.py tests/v1/streaming_input/test_async_llm_streaming.py  # passed\n```\n\nThe test file is covered by [Buildkite](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/64c5f14f6a89aff63bb9ea729a906a055caf00a7/.buildkite/test_areas/misc.yaml#L99-L118). In a local RTX A6000 replay using Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct, FlashAttention-2, asynchronous scheduling, and a 512-token context, the first stream chunk produced output; an oversized second chunk raised `VLLMValidationError`:\n\n| Observation | Unfixed | Fixed |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Final requests submitted after the error | 1 | 0 |\n| Tokens from a healthy same-engine follow-up | 4 | 4 |\n\nTo reproduce, yield a valid `StreamingInput`, wait for its first model output, then yield a chunk exceeding `max_model_len`; trace `_add_request` for the non-resumable `[0]`-token completion request. The replay was local, not CI, and does not claim output corruption or a current-main KVGuard detection. It used 64 KV blocks, `VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0` to avoid a local FlashInfer mismatch, and precompiled CUDA extensions from a nightly wheel five commits behind the tested main revision.\n\n## Details\n\n`handle_inputs()` already records whether input processing errored, but its `finally` block sent the completion request whenever the task was not cancelled. The fix also checks that error flag before finalizing. It adds no state, dependency, or synchronization and does not change input validation, model execution, sampling, or the public API. No user-facing docs or example change is needed.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
